<!-- Draft text. Every sentence here should be rewritten in Roy's own words. -->
<div class="eyebrow">The terms of this house</div>
<h1>Principles</h1>
<p class="standfirst">Six short promises, so that you know what you are reading and what is done with what you write.</p>
<ol class="roman">
<li><div class="num" aria-hidden="true">I</div><div class="txt"><h2>Written by a human</h2><p>Every sentence published under my name was written by me. Machines help me read and sort what I study. They do not write for me.</p></div></li>
<li><div class="num" aria-hidden="true">II</div><div class="txt"><h2>Grammar only</h2><p>English is not my first language. I let a machine check my grammar and nothing more. The phrasing stays mine, including where it is not idiomatic.</p></div></li>
<li><div class="num" aria-hidden="true">III</div><div class="txt"><h2>Questions, not applause</h2><p>There are no likes here. Select a sentence and question it. Readers are asked to write their own words too; what reads as generated will be removed at my discretion.</p></div></li>
<li><div class="num" aria-hidden="true">IV</div><div class="txt"><h2>Open to every reader</h2><p>Everything here is public, your questions included. Search engines and AI systems may read it. I use AI tools to help me read and analyse what readers send. I make no promise that the page is hidden from machines.</p></div></li>
<li><div class="num" aria-hidden="true">V</div><div class="txt"><h2>A sign-in and a handle</h2><p>That is all this site keeps about you. No password, no profile, no tracking script. The newsletter is a separate list you join and leave on your own, and it sends one digest a month.</p></div></li>
<li><div class="num" aria-hidden="true">VI</div><div class="txt"><h2>No promise of a reply</h2><p>Send in a link and say why it matters. I may write about it, fold it into an essay, or leave it. If I use it, I may say so in the piece.</p></div></li>
</ol>
<p class="signature"><%= (h (author-name)) %></p>
<p class="muted small" style="margin:4px 0 0">Last revised <time datetime="2026-11-11">11 November 2026</time></p>
</main>
